  "discussion": "The arrival of a moderate, long-period northwest swell will bring surf quickly building to advisory levels along north- and west-facing shores this morning. The swell peaks later today before beginning a decline on Monday. However, advisory level surf is expected to linger through at least Monday morning before falling to more moderate levels by Monday evening. Another advisory level northwest swell is possible Thursday into Friday, and moderate to large surf action appears to continue into the weekend. The current moderate, medium period south swell will hold today near seasonal average before declining on Monday. South shore surf will be tiny through much of the week with little southerly background energy reaching the islands. East-facing shores will see an increase in trade wind swell as northeast winds return today. Surf along east- facing shores will increase through Monday night and conditions will stay choppy as trades sustain through much of the week.",
